 "arc": "A calm two-count bounce that lives in the ankles. Weight settles over the character-right foot and the knees stay soft; the anticipation is a small sink into both heels, the action is one heel flicking out to the side while the opposite hip takes the weight, and the follow-through is the body rocking back to centre on the balls of both feet. Nothing travels — the floor pattern stays inside a single tile.\n\nThe arms are quiet and low, forearms held in front of the ribs at chest height and swinging only as much as the weight change carries them. Keep the shoulders down; this move reads relaxed, not bouncy.\n\nLoop seam: frame 15 returns to the same lifted-heel, weight-on-character-right shape as frame 0, so the cycle closes on a heel change rather than a landing. Both boundary frames are planted.",
